drm/xe: don't back up write-combined buffers on an integrated GPU

Under machine-wide memory reclaim, the bo shrinker backs up
non-purgeable buffers to shmem. On an integrated GPU most of a client's
private buffers are write-combined, and backing one up and reading it
back each change its pages' caching: set_pages_array_wc() on the read
back flushes every CPU's TLB per chunk, which is slow on a busy machine.
The read back happens in the client's next exec, in
xe_vm_validate_rebind under drm_gpuvm_exec_lock, with the reservations
of every buffer the exec uses held, its window's among them, so the
compositor's own commit, which locks that window, waits behind it.

On a Panther Lake laptop under a build, a compositor's main thread was
seen waiting 57 to 304 ms on such locks, held by the clients whose
windows it showed, each in ttm_tt_restore() and mostly in cpa_flush(),
and it missed frames for as long. Counting the buffers read back over
nine 30 s rounds found every one private, not exported, and nearly all
write-combined: in one round a client read back 105 write-combined
buffers in 223 ms, against 33 cached ones in under 1 ms. The few
hundred megabytes they take are worth keeping resident to spare the
desktop those stalls.

Skip a non-purgeable buffer that isn't cached on an integrated GPU.
Purgeable buffers are still purged, since their owner has said it can
recreate them, and discrete GPUs, whose system buffers back VRAM
evictions, are left as they were.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
@@ -1396,6 +1396,18 @@
 		goto out_unref;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Backing up a write-combined or uncached buffer, and reading it
+	 * back, change its pages' caching, which flushes every CPU's TLB.
+	 * The read back runs in the owner's next exec with the reservations
+	 * of its windows held, so a compositor waits behind it. On an
+	 * integrated GPU leave such buffers resident.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_DGFX(xe) && tt->caching != ttm_cached) {
+		lret = -EBUSY;
+		goto out_unref;
+	}
+
 	/* System CCS needs gpu copy when moving PL_TT -> PL_SYSTEM */
 	needs_rpm = (!IS_DGFX(xe) && bo->resource->mem_type != XE_PL_SYSTEM &&
 		     xe_bo_needs_ccs_pages(xe_bo));
